31
00:02:32,980 --> 00:02:40,780
At the last sentence of the first paragraph, we see Mr. Ford say, let me wrap up the presentation by summarizing my key points.

32
00:02:41,020 --> 00:02:42,860
So the phrase there is wrap up.

33
00:02:43,540 --> 00:02:46,260
It means to conclude, to finish, to end.

34
00:02:46,800 --> 00:02:51,720
This is the very end of his speech and so to wrap something up means to finish it.

35
00:02:52,220 --> 00:02:55,980
That's right. So maybe if you're giving a speech and someone is telling you to wrap it up quickly.

36
00:02:56,460 --> 00:02:57,460
That means stop.

37
00:02:57,460 --> 00:02:57,940
That's right.

38
00:02:58,460 --> 00:02:59,400
Please find an ending point.

39
00:02:59,920 --> 00:03:01,120
So wrap it up.

40
00:03:01,360 --> 00:03:01,780
Let's go.

41
00:03:02,060 --> 00:03:02,320
Come on.

42
00:03:03,060 --> 00:03:03,240
That's right.

43
00:03:03,660 --> 00:03:06,760
So he's wrapping it up by summarizing what he has talked about.

44
00:03:07,200 --> 00:03:12,140
And so he goes back to the very beginning and he says, as I mentioned at the outset.

45
00:03:12,860 --> 00:03:17,240
Okay, the outset is a noun, it's a time and it means the beginning.

46
00:03:17,900 --> 00:03:25,320
So you might remember in parts one or two of this speech that he was talking about why 2010 is an important year for their company.

47
00:03:25,860 --> 00:03:26,860
And so this is the outset.

48
00:03:27,160 --> 00:03:33,440
This is the beginning. You can also say at the outset things looked bad but it turns out that they went well.

49
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:34,360
Okay.

50
00:03:34,400 --> 00:03:38,060
So outset means beginning the start of something.

51
00:03:38,730 --> 00:03:39,050
Okay.

52
00:03:39,530 --> 00:03:43,610
And he also talked about how the computer industry demand is booming.

53
00:03:44,660 --> 00:03:50,560
All right. So booming is an interesting word because boom, the noun means boom, a sound.

54
00:03:50,580 --> 00:03:51,580
To explode.

55
00:03:51,580 --> 00:03:53,500
Right. It's a sound that you hear when there's a storm.

56
00:03:54,180 --> 00:03:56,320
But booming means doing very well.

57
00:03:56,880 --> 00:03:59,120
That means that in this case demand is booming.

58
00:03:59,460 --> 00:04:01,060
There is a lot of demand.

59
00:04:01,560 --> 00:04:05,240
That's right. So when you hear people say business is booming.

60
00:04:06,040 --> 00:04:07,440
That means business is going very well.

61
00:04:07,640 --> 00:04:08,300
It's very successful.

62
00:04:09,220 --> 00:04:14,480
Okay. So it basically means that it's doing very well, that it's growing quickly and rapidly.

63
00:04:15,580 --> 00:04:26,930
So he went on to talk about the X420 and how the company has plans to keep expanding and keep coming out with ever more revolutionary and impressive products.

64
00:04:27,380 --> 00:04:27,830
Okay.

65
00:04:28,030 --> 00:04:32,030
So something is a revolutionary if it changes a situation.

66
00:04:32,430 --> 00:04:32,650
Okay.

67
00:04:33,270 --> 00:04:37,650
Because revolution basically means change but not a small change, a really big change.

68
00:04:38,270 --> 00:04:43,370
And so a product is revolutionary if it introduces something really new, really exciting.

69
00:04:43,810 --> 00:04:44,150
Okay.

70
00:04:44,150 --> 00:04:48,370
So an example of a revolutionary product was the home computer.

71
00:04:48,790 --> 00:04:49,330
Exactly.

72
00:04:49,610 --> 00:05:00,070
Because the home computer changed the way people typed and communicated and did all these different things. And so it's revolutionary because it introduced a big change.

73
00:05:00,780 --> 00:05:01,270
That's right. Okay.

74
00:05:01,430 --> 00:05:02,290
So revolutionary.

75
00:05:03,550 --> 00:05:14,420
Towards the end of Mr. Ford's dialogue, he said that they're going to have a Q&A section and he left us with a quote that according to him sums up everything we've discussed today.

76
00:05:14,420 --> 00:05:15,980
Okay. To sum up.

77
00:05:16,240 --> 00:05:28,340
This is very related to the word to summarize. It means to say in fewer words. Okay. So this quote says what he wants to say, but it says it in a very short space.

78
00:05:28,900 --> 00:05:35,070
So if we read a book and I ask you to sum up the story, this is basically I'm asking for a summary.

79
00:05:35,740 --> 00:05:43,810
That's right. So I could say, you know, the Harry Potter story is a story about a young boy who is a wizard who loses his parents, who goes to school with his friends and learns about his powers.

80
00:05:45,220 --> 00:05:47,650
That's a perfect way to sum up the Harry Potter story.

