00:07:49,900 --> 00:07:58,650
So the first phrase we've got here in Fluency Builder is an interesting one, and I think it's important to point out because we've got a verb and a noun that often go together.

105
00:07:59,540 --> 00:08:06,490
Mr. Ford said this kind of computer can really satisfy those needs that customers have.

106
00:08:07,180 --> 00:08:07,310
That's right.

107
00:08:07,610 --> 00:08:10,430
So the phrase there is to satisfy a need.

108
00:08:10,770 --> 00:08:13,470
