109
00:08:13,630 --> 00:08:15,830
You want to satisfy your customers' needs.

110
00:08:16,470 --> 00:08:17,890
All right, so what do I need?

111
00:08:18,150 --> 00:08:30,500
I need a good computer that is fast that I can do my business on. And this computer, the X420, satisfies that need. It does what I need it to do.

112
00:08:30,500 --> 00:08:43,420
Okay, so we understand the verb to satisfy, but the phrase is a very powerful phrase, especially if you use it in business where you're saying we are giving our customers what they need and we are making them happy.

113
00:08:43,420 --> 00:08:44,420
Exactly.

114
00:08:44,420 --> 00:08:48,940
